prompt loop card: take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first; approve your own design rounds and make progress; double-seat visions; send often
think The Braid journey closed clean this arc (r1 crux · r2 bron · r3 knot · r4 true), all four rungs GREEN on both remotes, REMEMBER folded. Reading the frontier: the Mycelium road has now built two of TigerBeetle's three signature primitives — the two-phase transfer (Pledge) and the linked chain (Braid). The third, the pending-transfer timeout, is unbuilt and is the next Lindy-first crux on the whole road.
think Crux-first: the hardest still-tractable move is a deadline measured in the order's own clock, not the wall — a reservation the ledger itself lapses when the committed order passes a position, decided identically by every honest node because the order is deterministic. This introduces something genuinely new to the tree: honesty across the ABSENCE of a fact by a deadline, where every prior ledger decided on a fact that arrived. It composes cord + fold + kumara public API only, editing none — the same additive discipline Tenure · Till · Purse · Pledge · Braid each kept.
think Named the journey Lapse (grepped the tree: no collision in .rye/.rish) — a plain, warm accounting/legal word for a reservation expiring unexercised, kin to Cord · Knot · Till · Purse · Pledge · Braid (Comlink tendency: clearest warm safe word). The deadline rides inside the signed pledge body (P · id · deadline(8) · to), so it cannot be moved after the signature; a deadline not strictly after its opening position is expired at birth and refuses BadDeadline.
obs No code this round — a self-approved design read, its own signed increment per the send-often instruction. The arc is the seated rhythm: r1 crux (lapse.rye) · r2 travels (lapse_bron.rye) · r3 across a Knot (lapse_knot.rye) · r4 true to the bytes (lapse_true.rye + fixture_gen + awk). Verified the frontier GREEN first: mycelium_braid_witness ran GREEN before opening the next journey.
file active-designing/20260813-085046_mycelium-lapse-pending-timeout-exploration.md the self-approved design read opening the Lapse arc; names the crux, the deadline-in-the-order clock, the four verdicts, and the r1–r4 rhythm
recommend keep-going the Lapse arc is read and open; next agent-doable lap is r1 — mycelium/lapse.rye + tools/mycelium_lapse_witness.rish, the deadline verdict folded over a code-seated scene, GREEN then sent as its own round. A served lapse · per-account mint authority · breach renames (cairn-first) · deep debride · seed force-push stay the maintainer's hand.
